//video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2091355855895527424/pl/nRuXWeXAjtPbmwn8.m3u8?v=bb6", "aspectRatio": [115, 204], "heightRatio": 177, "type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2091355855895527424/vid/avc1/320x566/UVIkrCFc5p6OMhWi.mp4"}, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2072361354237734912/ojuHRLVk_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Jayroo", "username": "jayroo69"}, "content": "Shameless", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 33}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCNRd4fT", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 36, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8793993, "raw_content": "...No Jesus, No peace...Know Jesus, Know Peace...\n\nI rejoice at Your word as one who finds great treasure. \u2014Psalm 119:162\n\nThru the Bible - Questions & Answers  Dr. J. Vernon McGee\n\nCould Jesus have sinned?\n\nhttps://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-questions-and-answers/?ref=sc\n\nhttps://ttb.org/\n\nThru the Bible - Minute with McGee   Dr. J. Vernon McGee\n\nHave confidence\n\nThe future promise of blessing rests upon the solid history of the past when God delivered them from Egypt, you see. He said, \u201cNow I have done this for you; don\u2019t you know I will do it for you in the future?\u201d And that\u2019s what He tells us today. \u201cBeing confident of this very thing, that He which hath begun a good work in you\u2026.\u201d Has God blessed you, friend, and brought you up to this moment? Why do you think He\u2019s going to let you down? Well, you can be confident of this very thing\u2014that He that has brought you up to this very moment, why, He\u2019s going to lead you right through to \u201cthe day of Jesus Christ.\u201d\n\nhttps://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-minute-with-mcgee/listen/have-confidence-1289973.html\n\nhttps://ttb.org/\n\n___\n\nDaily Promises\n\nTeaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, [even] unto the end of the world. Amen. (Matthew 28:20)\n\nJesus promised that He will always be with us, even to the end of the age. We as Christians have Christ as our authority and comfort. He is the Emmanuel (the God who came to earth to live with us) and though He has ascended to the Father, even so, He remains to live with us.\n\nhttps://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/promises/view.cfm\n\n___\n\nFollowing God the first time\n\nTo every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven. -- Ecclesiastes 3:1\n\nIt's much easier to follow God the first time than to have to turn around and start over again.\n\nhttps://digginganotherwell.substack.com/p/following-god-the-first-time\n\n___\n\nC. H. Spurgeon's Evening Reading (August 22nd)\n\n\"The unsearchable riches of Christ.\" \u2014 Ephesians 3:8\n\nhttps://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?Time=pm\n\n___\n\nC. H. Spurgeon's Morning Reading (August 23rd)\n\n\"The voice of weeping shall be no more heard.\" \u2014 Isaiah 65:19\n\nhttps://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?doy=236\n\n\n\n\n...Faith Plus Nothing Equals Salvation...\n\nhttps://youtu.be/fDR0mu18x80?si=aG5gQZZ3noLTFzQk\n\nhttps://blueletterbible.org/Comm/mcgee_j_vernon/eBooks/faith-plus-zero-equals-salvation.cfm\n\n\u201cThe sin underneath all our sins is to trust the lie of the serpent that we cannot trust the love and grace of Christ and must take matters into our own hands\u201d\n\nMartin Luther", "author": "ashlanddog", "created": 1787449708514, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Landslide_2020", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "...No Jesus, No peace...Know Jesus, Know Peace...", "last_comment_created": 1787450000255, "content": "<p>...No Jesus, No peace...Know Jesus, Know Peace...</p>\n<p>I rejoice at Your word as one who finds great treasure. \u2014Psalm 119:162</p>\n<p>Thru the Bible - Questions &amp; Answers  Dr. J. Vernon McGee</p>\n<p>Could Jesus have sinned?</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-questions-and-answers/?ref=sc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-questions-and-answers/?ref=sc</a></p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://ttb.org/\" target=\"_blank\">https://ttb.org/</a></p>\n<p>Thru the Bible - Minute with McGee   Dr. J. Vernon McGee</p>\n<p>Have confidence</p>\n<p>The future promise of blessing rests upon the solid history of the past when God delivered them from Egypt, you see. He said, \u201cNow I have done this for you; don\u2019t you know I will do it for you in the future?\u201d And that\u2019s what He tells us today. \u201cBeing confident of this very thing, that He which hath begun a good work in you\u2026.\u201d Has God blessed you, friend, and brought you up to this moment? Why do you think He\u2019s going to let you down? Well, you can be confident of this very thing\u2014that He that has brought you up to this very moment, why, He\u2019s going to lead you right through to \u201cthe day of Jesus Christ.\u201d</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-minute-with-mcgee/listen/have-confidence-1289973.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.oneplace.com/ministries/thru-the-bible-minute-with-mcgee/listen/have-confidence-1289973.html</a></p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://ttb.org/\" target=\"_blank\">https://ttb.org/</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p>Daily Promises</p>\n<p>Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, [even] unto the end of the world. Amen. (Matthew 28:20)</p>\n<p>Jesus promised that He will always be with us, even to the end of the age. We as Christians have Christ as our authority and comfort. He is the Emmanuel (the God who came to earth to live with us) and though He has ascended to the Father, even so, He remains to live with us.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/promises/view.cfm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/promises/view.cfm</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p>Following God the first time</p>\n<p>To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven. -- Ecclesiastes 3:1</p>\n<p>It's much easier to follow God the first time than to have to turn around and start over again.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://digginganotherwell.substack.com/p/following-god-the-first-time\" target=\"_blank\">https://digginganotherwell.substack.com/p/following-god-the-first-time</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p>C. H. Spurgeon's Evening Reading (August 22nd)</p>\n<p>&quot;The unsearchable riches of Christ.&quot; \u2014 Ephesians 3:8</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?Time=pm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?Time=pm</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p>C. H. Spurgeon's Morning Reading (August 23rd)</p>\n<p>&quot;The voice of weeping shall be no more heard.&quot; \u2014 Isaiah 65:19</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?doy=236\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.blueletterbible.org/devotionals/me/view.cfm?doy=236</a></p>\n<p>...Faith Plus Nothing Equals Salvation...</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fDR0mu18x80?si=aG5gQZZ3noLTFzQk\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/fDR0mu18x80?si=aG5gQZZ3noLTFzQk</a></p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://blueletterbible.org/Comm/mcgee_j_vernon/eBooks/faith-plus-zero-equals-salvation.cfm\" target=\"_blank\">https://blueletterbible.org/Comm/mcgee_j_vernon/eBooks/faith-plus-zero-equals-salvation.cfm</a></p>\n<p>\u201cThe sin underneath all our sins is to trust the lie of the serpent that we cannot trust the love and grace of Christ and must take matters into our own hands\u201d</p>\n<p>Martin Luther</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 36, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCNSjGfG", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8794176, "raw_content": "", "author": "Oodles", "created": 1787458480286, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "WeWillRideAgain", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.foxnews.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCNSjGfG.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.foxnews.com/media/mark-ruffalo-fires-back-paramount-appalling-antisemitism-accusation-ellison-merger-criticism", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Left-wing actor now nose who he is not allowed to criticize ", "last_comment_created": 1787484305893, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 6, "score_up": 23, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Mark Ruffalo fires back at Paramount's antisemitism accusation, calling it \"appalling and fundamentally dishonest\" amid the Warner Bros. Discovery merger.", "large_image": 